---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../data/author.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who writes AIBuilderHub, what I've actually built with these tools, and how I make money from this site."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
      <img
        src={AUTHOR.photo}
        alt={AUTHOR.name}
        width="80"
        height="80"
        class="rounded-full object-cover shrink-0"
      />
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold" style="color: var(--color-text);">{AUTHOR.name}</h1>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted);">{AUTHOR.role}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose max-w-none">

      <p>Most reviews of AI tools are useless. They're written by people who've never opened the product, padded with SEO keywords, and ranked based on commission rates rather than actual quality.</p>

      {AUTHOR.longBio.map(paragraph => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>I build real projects with every tool I review - landing pages, SaaS MVPs, automations - and report what actually happens. Including what breaks, what's confusing, and what the marketing page doesn't tell you.</p>

      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>People who want to build digital products with AI but don't have time to test 30 different platforms. Specifically: solopreneurs launching their first product, freelancers adding AI capabilities to their services, and small business owners who want internal tools without an IT budget.</p>

      <h2>How I make money</h2>
      <p>Through affiliate commissions when you click my links and sign up for tools. I disclose this on every article. It doesn't change my rankings - a tool I don't recommend stays off the list regardless of commission rate. See the <a href="/disclosure">full affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, or want to suggest a tool to review: <strong>{AUTHOR.email}</strong>
        {AUTHOR.sameAs.length > 0 && (
          <>
            {' · '}
            {AUTHOR.sameAs.map((link, i) => (
              <>
                {i > 0 && ' · '}
                <a href={link.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{link.label}</a>
              </>
            ))}
          </>
        )}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
